\f0\fs24 \cf0 This is a case study on how I would develop and market an exhibition for the late Akira Toriyama. One thing I wanted to do differently with this study was to focus on how toriyama became the legend of his field rather than focusing on the more popular series that he is now known for, dragon ball.\
\
Additionally I wanted to limit myself to a very strict color palette of black, white and gold in order to allude to the traditional black and white inked panels of a manga, and pay homage to the warm yellow that he would later paint his studio/home.\
\
This provided natural challenges as there was less public material of his earlier works to highlight for an exhibition and making any materials associated with this exhibition interested by focusing primarily on form and in a sense shadow rather than using vibrant and robust color palettes.\
\
For this case study I planned a floor plan inside of the Honolulu museum of modern art. Staff, vip and guest badges for the exhibition, merchandise. Invitations and mobile app that visitors would be able to use during this exhibition.}